// Test: call arguments are evaluated left to right, exactly once each.
//
// Nothing in functions/ could see this: the callee receives the same values in
// the same slots whatever order they were computed in, and a function that is
// called twice returns the same answer the second time. Only an argument whose
// evaluation prints separates the cases.
uno() {
    >> "[1]"
    <~ 1
}

dos() {
    >> "[2]"
    <~ 2
}

tres() {
    >> "[3]"
    <~ 3
}

suma(a, b, c) {
    <~ a + b + c
}

>> "total:" suma(uno(), dos(), tres()) ¶

// Twice in one call: an engine that caches by expression shape would print
// `[1]` once.
>> "doble:" suma(uno(), uno(), dos()) ¶
